<LegalServiceLayout title="Wisconsin Guardian ad Litem Services" description="Patrick Rowe provides court-appointed Guardian ad Litem services for children and vulnerable adults in Wisconsin family and probate proceedings." canonicalPath="/legal-services/guardian-ad-litem" breadcrumbLabel="Guardian ad Litem" headline="Wisconsin Guardian ad Litem (GAL) Services" subheadline="Protecting and advocating for the best interests of children and vulnerable adults in family and probate courts." ctaHeading="Discuss a Wisconsin GAL appointment.">
  <section class="container-shell py-16 sm:py-24" aria-labelledby="role-title"><div class="max-w-4xl"><h2 id="role-title" class="text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">What is a Guardian ad Litem?</h2><p class="mt-7 text-lg leading-9 text-onyx/80">A Guardian ad Litem is an attorney appointed by the court to fulfill an independent statutory role. The GAL investigates relevant facts, evaluates the individual’s best interests, and provides advocacy and recommendations to the court. The exact duties depend on the proceeding and the appointment order.</p><p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-9 text-onyx/80">This work involves objective factual investigation and careful review of the circumstances affecting a child or vulnerable adult. A GAL’s best-interest recommendation informs the court; the judge makes the decision. A GAL is not a parent’s personal attorney or a substitute for an appointed guardian.</p></div></section>
  <section class="border-y border-forest/15 bg-forest/5 py-16 sm:py-24" aria-labelledby="appointments-title"><div class="container-shell"><h2 id="appointments-title" class="text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">How I Accept GAL Appointments</h2><ol class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2"><li class="border-t-2 border-gold bg-parchment p-7 sm:p-9"><span class="eyebrow text-forest/65">01</span><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl text-forest">Court Appointments</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-onyx/80">Patrick accepts assignments directly through Wisconsin circuit court judges or family court commissioners, subject to the applicable appointment procedures, eligibility requirements, and conflict review.</p></li><li class="border-t-2 border-gold bg-parchment p-7 sm:p-9"><span class="eyebrow text-forest/65">02</span><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl text-forest">Party Stipulations</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-onyx/80">Parents or their attorneys may mutually nominate Patrick when they need a seasoned, detail-oriented professional. An agreed nomination remains subject to court approval and a formal appointment; private agreement alone does not create GAL authority.</p></li></ol></div></section>
</LegalServiceLayout>
